<link rel="stylesheet" href="<%= cachebust('/stylesheets/design.css') %>">

<%# Swatch values are read from the live stylesheet by the script at the bottom %>
<% sections = {
     'colour' => %w[Colour Colour],
     'type' => %w[Type Typography],
     'shape' => ['Shape', 'Radius, elevation, spacing'],
     'layout' => ['Layout', 'Page shell'],
     'components' => %w[Components Components],
     'theming' => %w[Theming Theming]
   }
   section_head = lambda do |id, intro = nil|
     %(<div class="d-flex flex-column gap-1 border-top border-2 border-dark pt-3">
         <div class="spec fw-bold">#{format('%02d', sections.keys.index(id) + 1)}</div>
         <h2 class="m-0">#{sections[id].last}</h2>
         #{%(<p class="m-0 text-body-secondary" style="max-width: 680px">#{intro}</p>) if intro}
       </div>)
   end
   subhead = lambda do |title, note = nil|
     %(<div class="d-flex align-items-baseline flex-wrap gap-2"><h3 class="m-0">#{title}</h3>#{%(<span class="text-body-secondary">#{note}</span>) if note}</div>)
   end

   # Run through clamp_color as /theme.css does, so a colour too light for white text is darkened
   themed_colors = %w[#1a73e8 #ffc107].map { |color| [color, clamp_color(color)] }

   flashes = [['primary', 'Your ticket is booked.', 'View order'], ['warning', 'Only 3 tickets left.', 'Book now'], ['danger', 'Payment failed.', 'Try again']] %>

<div class="design-guide d-flex flex-column gap-5" style="max-width: 1080px">

  <header class="d-flex flex-column gap-3" style="max-width: 720px">
    <div class="spec text-uppercase fw-bold">Design guide · v1 · October 2026</div>
    <h1 class="m-0">Dandelion</h1>
    <p class="m-0 readable">The visual language of dandelion.events as it exists in code today. This page is rendered with the site's own <code>app.css</code> and <code>bootstrap5.css</code>, so swatches, type and components are the real thing. The site is Bootstrap 5.3.8, restyled through its variables.</p>
    <p class="m-0 small text-body-secondary">The root font size is 17px (19px from 1680px, 21px from 1920px), so rem values scale with the viewport. Sizes are in rem (or em, to follow the text); px is kept for 1–2px hairlines, the containers' 15px side padding (<code>$container-padding-x</code>) and overrides that must line up with Google Maps. Colour values, radii and type sizes are measured live; other sizes are copied from the stylesheets.</p>
    <nav class="d-flex flex-wrap gap-2">
      <% sections.each do |id, (title, _)| %>
        <a class="btn btn-outline-primary btn-sm" href="#<%= id %>"><%= title %></a>
      <% end %>
    </nav>
  </header>

  <!-- COLOUR -->
  <section id="colour">
    <%== section_head.call('colour') %>

    <div class="d-flex flex-column gap-3">
      <%== subhead.call('Theme', 'A ramp generated from one value with <code>oklch()</code>. Components use the 500, 400 as the gradient end, 600 for hover, 50 to 200 for alert and toast backgrounds, and 800 for text on those tints. Organisations and events set <code>--theme-500</code> only (through <code>/theme.css</code>). Tints (50–200) sit at fixed lightness, so they look equally light across hues; shades (400–800) are relative to the 500, with 800 capped dark enough for text on tints.') %>
      <%= partial :'stats/design/ramp', locals: {
            prefix: '--theme',
            label: '--theme-*',
            label_note: "Primary and success · follows each organisation's theme",
            notes: {
              '50' => 'alert and toast background',
              '200' => 'alert and toast gradient end',
              '400' => 'button gradient end',
              '500' => nil,
              '600' => 'hover',
              '800' => 'text on tints'
            },
            sample_class: 'alert alert-primary',
            sample_title: 'Primary alerts and toasts',
            sample_to: '200'
          } %>
      <div class="small text-body-secondary">Bootstrap's <code>rgba(var(--bs-*-rgb))</code> colours need an rgb triplet, so <code>/theme.css</code> also sets <code>--theme-500-rgb</code>.</div>
    </div>

    <div class="d-flex flex-column gap-3">
      <%== subhead.call('Lavender', "The default site's AI well and <code>.gradient</code> backgrounds, with the theme ramp's steps derived from --color-lavender-500, which has the default green's lightness and chroma. Themed pages switch the AI well to the theme.") %>
      <%= partial :'stats/design/ramp', locals: {
            prefix: '--color-lavender',
            notes: {
              '50' => '.gradient, AI well background',
              '200' => 'not used yet',
              '400' => 'AI well gradient end',
              '500' => 'not used yet',
              '600' => 'features and Luma pages: purple divider end, call-to-action glow',
              '800' => 'not used yet'
            },
            sample_class: 'ai-well',
            sample_title: 'AI well',
            sample_to: '400'
          } %>
    </div>

    <div class="d-flex flex-column gap-3">
      <%== subhead.call('Warning and danger', "Two families, used the same way as the theme ramp: each variant class (alert-warning, toast-warning, table-warning, btn-warning, text-bg-warning and the danger ones) sets its steps as <code>--variant-50</code> to <code>--variant-800</code>, and each component maps those to its roles once. The 500 is also Bootstrap's <code>$warning</code> and <code>$danger</code> in bootstrap5.scss, so text-danger, form errors and the like match. There are no warning buttons yet, so --color-orange-600 is unused.") %>
      <% roles = {
           '50' => 'alert, toast and row background',
           '200' => 'tint gradient end, row border',
           '400' => 'gradient end',
           '500' => 'fill: badges, buttons',
           '600' => 'button hover',
           '800' => 'text and border on tints'
         }
         other_uses = {
           'orange' => {
             '500' => 'ASN stats: bot % of 30 and over',
             '400' => 'star icons, feedback stars, map areas, features page',
             '200' => 'features page divider end'
           },
           'red' => {
             '500' => 'ASN stats: bot % of 60 and over; check-in QR scan line',
             '400' => 'map: event and organisation markers'
           }
         } %>
      <% [%w[Warning orange warning], %w[Danger red danger]].each do |title, colour, variant| %>
        <%= partial :'stats/design/ramp', locals: {
              prefix: "--color-#{colour}",
              label: title,
              label_note: "--color-#{colour}-*",
              notes: roles.merge(other_uses[colour]) { |_, role, uses| "#{role}. Also: #{uses}" },
              sample_class: "alert alert-#{variant}",
              sample_title: "#{title} alerts and toasts",
              sample_to: '200'
            } %>
      <% end %>
      <div class="small text-body-secondary">Alerts and toasts: a sheen from the 50 to the 200. table-warning and table-danger rows: the 50, with the 200 for borders and a mix 30% of the way to it on hover.</div>
    </div>

    <div class="d-flex flex-column gap-3">
      <%== subhead.call('Greys, black and white', "Bootstrap's own variables, set in bootstrap5.scss to warm greys: Bootstrap's lightness steps at a slight warm hue (oklch hue 75, chroma .006–.008). The cool --color-canvas behind them on body.canvas pages is deliberate. Usage: 100 wells and hovered dropdown and list items · 200 hovered nav links, autocomplete items and table rows, and stripes · 300 table borders · 400 input borders and hr · 600 secondary text · 700 input add-ons · 800 search bar · 900 header and sidebar. Body text is <code>--bs-body-color</code>, the same as 900. Black and white with transparency use <code>rgba(var(--bs-black-rgb), a)</code> and <code>rgba(var(--bs-white-rgb), a)</code>, e.g. shadows, hairlines and image overlays.") %>
      <div class="row g-3">
        <% %w[--bs-white --bs-gray-100 --bs-gray-200 --bs-gray-300 --bs-gray-400 --bs-gray-500 --bs-gray-600 --bs-gray-700 --bs-gray-800 --bs-gray-900 --bs-black].each do |name| %>
          <%= partial :'stats/design/swatch', locals: { vars: [name], col: 'col-6 col-md-3 col-xl' } %>
        <% end %>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="d-flex flex-column gap-3">
      <%== subhead.call('Accents and surfaces', 'Each accent has one role. The dark header and sidebar are a sunset: near-black fading to --color-midnight, with the orange-to-yellow --gradient-active as the sun on the active sidebar item, the notification dot and the load bar. Light content marks active states with the theme colour, so there is one active colour per surface. On the default site purple also marks AI and calendar events; themed pages switch those to the theme. --gradient-rainbow is only for .gradient-text headlines on marketing pages and the signed-out home.') %>
      <div class="row g-3 row-cols-2 row-cols-md-3 row-cols-xl-5">
        <% [
             [%w[--color-paper], '.gradient end'],
             [%w[--color-canvas], 'body.canvas'],
             [%w[--color-highlight], 'mark'],
             [%w[--color-yellow-500 --color-yellow-400], 'text-bg-yellow: Featured, Co-host, rota points; contributions chart (500)'],
             [%w[--color-midnight], 'header sunset; AI and calendar events on the default site']
           ].each do |vars, note| %>
          <%= partial :'stats/design/swatch', locals: { vars: vars, note: note } %>
        <% end %>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="d-flex flex-column gap-3">
      <%== subhead.call('Other gradients') %>
      <div class="row g-3 row-cols-1 row-cols-sm-2 row-cols-xl-4">
        <% [
             { box_class: 'gradient', title: '.gradient', note: 'Lavender to paper. body.gradient on the sign-in, sign-up and auth failure pages; a .gradient div, which also fades to white at the bottom, behind the hero on the marketing pages and the signed-out home.' },
             { fills: ['var(--gradient-active)'], title: '--gradient-active', note: 'Sidebar active item, notification dot, page-load bar.' },
             { fills: ['var(--gradient-rainbow)'], title: '--gradient-rainbow', note: '.gradient-text only.' },
             { fills: ['var(--gradient-header)'], title: '--gradient-header', note: 'The header: 45°, --bs-gray-900 to 66%, then midnight.' }
           ].each do |swatch| %>
          <%= partial :'stats/design/swatch', locals: swatch %>
        <% end %>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="d-flex flex-column gap-3">
      <%== subhead.call('Marketing pages', 'The features and comparison pages. Their purple gradient and the five reason colours on the Luma page are derived from <code>--color-midnight</code> and <code>--color-magenta-500</code>.') %>
      <div class="row g-3 row-cols-2 row-cols-md-3 row-cols-xl-5">
        <% [
             { vars: %w[--wash-amber --wash-rose --wash-magenta --wash-purple], note: 'section backgrounds: the 50 step of orange, rose, magenta and lavender' },
             { vars: %w[--color-rose-500 --color-rose-200], note: 'section divider: 500 to 200' },
             { vars: %w[--color-magenta-500 --color-magenta-200], note: 'section divider: 500 to 200' },
             { fills: 0.step(100, 25).map { |pct| "color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-magenta-500), var(--color-midnight) #{pct}%)" }, title: 'Magenta to midnight', note: 'color-mix, 0–100%' }
           ].each do |swatch| %>
          <%= partial :'stats/design/swatch', locals: swatch %>
        <% end %>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="d-flex flex-column gap-3">
      <%== subhead.call('Third-party brands', 'Only for buttons and labels that stand for these services.') %>
      <div class="row g-3 row-cols-2 row-cols-md-3 row-cols-xl-5">
        <% [
             [%w[--color-evm], 'EVM'],
             [%w[--color-stripe], 'Stripe · text-bg-stripe'],
             [%w[--color-opencollective], 'Open Collective'],
             [%w[--color-coinbase], 'Coinbase'],
             [%w[--color-signal --color-signal-dark], 'Signal · btn-signal'],
             [%w[--color-paypal], 'PayPal'],
             [%w[--color-gocardless --color-gocardless-text], 'GoCardless'],
             [%w[--color-mollie], 'Mollie']
           ].each do |vars, note| %>
          <%= partial :'stats/design/swatch', locals: { vars: vars, fills: ["var(#{vars.first})"], title: vars.first, note: note } %>
        <% end %>
      </div>
      <div class="d-flex flex-wrap gap-2 align-items-center">
        <span class="small text-body-secondary">Payment badges, from <code>badge-payment-&lt;method&gt;</code>:</span>
        <% [%w[coinbase Coinbase], %w[mollie Mollie], %w[paypal PayPal], ['gocardless-instant', 'GoCardless'], ['gocardless-instalment', 'GoCardless instalments'], ['opencollective', 'OC: …'], ['evm', 'EVM: …']].each do |name, text| %>
          <span class="badge badge-payment-<%= name %>"><%= text %></span>
        <% end %>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- TYPE -->
  <section id="type">
    <%== section_head.call('type') %>

    <div class="row g-4">
      <div class="col-lg-6">
        <div class="border rounded p-4 h-100 d-flex flex-column gap-3">
          <div class="spec fw-bold">HEADINGS · --header-font-family</div>
          <div class="header-font display-5 fw-bold lh-1">Hanken Grotesk</div>
          <div class="small text-body-secondary">Variable 100–900, used at bold. Letter-spacing −0.02em. Also <code>.strapline</code> and <code>.header-font</code>.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="col-lg-6">
        <div class="border rounded p-4 h-100 d-flex flex-column gap-3">
          <div class="spec fw-bold">BODY · --body-font-family</div>
          <div class="display-5 lh-1">Plus Jakarta Sans</div>
          <div class="small text-body-secondary">Default weight 500, labels 700, bold for <code>b</code>/<code>strong</code>. Line height 1.45.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="d-flex flex-column gap-3">
      <%== subhead.call('Scale') %>
      <div class="border-bottom">
        <% [
             ['h1 · .fs-1', '--font-size-3xl · 2rem', '<h1 data-sample class="m-0">Gatherings near you</h1>'],
             ['h2 · .fs-2', '--font-size-2xl · 1.66rem', '<h2 data-sample class="m-0">Gatherings near you</h2>'],
             ['h3 · .fs-3', '--font-size-xl · 1.4rem', '<h3 data-sample class="m-0">Your upcoming events</h3>'],
             ['h4 · .fs-4', '--font-size-lg · 1.125rem', '<h4 data-sample class="m-0">Upcoming birthdays</h4>'],
             ['h5 · .fs-5', '--font-size-md · .875rem', '<h5 data-sample class="m-0">Ticket types</h5>'],
             ['.readable', '--font-size-base · 1rem', '<div data-sample class="readable">Long-form copy such as event descriptions sets at 1rem.</div>'],
             ['nav · .btn', '--font-size-md · .875rem', '<span data-sample class="btn btn-outline-primary">Buttons, nav links and tabs</span>'],
             ['body · h6 · .fs-6', '--font-size-sm · .825rem', '<div data-sample>Body text, inputs, tables, dropdown items</div>'],
             ['.small', '.875em of its context', '<span data-sample class="small">Secondary details: a location, a description</span>'],
             ['.badge', '.875em of its context', '<span data-sample class="badge text-bg-secondary">Badges</span>'],
             ['.breadcrumb', '--font-size-xs · .75rem', '<ol data-sample class="breadcrumb m-0"><li class="breadcrumb-item">Breadcrumbs</li><li class="breadcrumb-item">and carets</li></ol>']
           ].each do |name, size, sample| %>
          <div data-spec-row class="py-3 border-top">
            <div class="row align-items-baseline">
              <code class="col-md-2 spec"><%= name %></code>
              <div class="col-md-7"><%== sample %></div>
              <code class="col-md-3 spec"><%= size %> · <span data-px></span></code>
            </div>
          </div>
        <% end %>
      </div>
      <div class="small text-body-secondary"><code>.h1</code>–<code>.h6</code> give any element a heading's style, e.g. <code>&lt;h4 class="h2"&gt;</code> for block titles. The heading sizes are set in bootstrap5.scss (<code>$h1-font-size</code>…), so <code>.fs-1</code>–<code>.fs-6</code> make text a heading's size without its weight or font. <code>.small</code> shrinks text to .875em of its context; it's Bootstrap's class for smaller text without the meaning of <code>&lt;small&gt;</code>, which is for small print. Secondary text is --bs-gray-600 (<code>.subtle</code>, form-text).</div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- SHAPE -->
  <section id="shape">
    <%== section_head.call('shape') %>

    <div class="d-flex flex-column gap-3">
      <%== subhead.call('Radius', "Bootstrap's radius variables, set to four steps in <code>bootstrap5.scss</code>. Square corners (0) where an element sits flush against another; 50% for circles.") %>
      <div class="row g-3">
        <% [
             ['--bs-border-radius', 'Buttons, inputs, cards, badges, labels, pagination, sidebar pills. -sm is the same'],
             ['--bs-border-radius-lg', 'Menus and panels: dropdowns, autocomplete, cookie banner, AI well, ask box'],
             ['--bs-border-radius-xl', 'Mobile bottom sheet (top corners), marketing cards'],
             ['--bs-border-radius-pill', 'Nav crumbs, avatars, round buttons and dots']
           ].each do |name, note| %>
          <div class="col-6 col-md-3">
            <div class="bg-body-secondary border mb-2" style="height: 72px; border-radius: var(<%= name %>)"></div>
            <div class="fw-bold text-break"><%= name %></div>
            <div class="spec"><span data-css-value="<%= name %>"></span></div>
            <div class="small text-body-secondary"><%= note %></div>
          </div>
        <% end %>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="d-flex flex-column gap-3">
      <%== subhead.call('Elevation', "Bootstrap's three shadows, used through its variables or the <code>shadow-sm</code>, <code>shadow</code> and <code>shadow-lg</code> classes.") %>
      <div class="bg-body-tertiary rounded p-4">
        <div class="row g-4">
          <% [
               ['--bs-box-shadow-sm', 'Resting surfaces: header, search, cards, editor toolbar'],
               ['--bs-box-shadow', 'Floating: dropdowns, autocomplete, cookie banner, chat, hover lift'],
               ['--bs-box-shadow-lg', 'Not used yet']
             ].each do |name, note| %>
            <div class="col-md-4">
              <div class="bg-white rounded p-3 small h-100" style="box-shadow: var(<%= name %>)"><b><%= name %></b><br><%= note %></div>
            </div>
          <% end %>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="small text-body-secondary">The mobile event page's fixed tickets bar keeps its own upward shadow.</div>
    </div>

    <div class="d-flex flex-column gap-3">
      <%== subhead.call('Spacing') %>
      <div class="row gx-4 row-cols-1 row-cols-md-2 row-cols-xl-3">
        <% [
             ['Content padding', '1.5625rem · mobile .9375rem'],
             ['Grid gutter', '.75rem'],
             ['Container padding', '15px each side'],
             ['Card body', '1.25rem'],
             ['Card header', '.75rem 1.25rem'],
             ['Field spacing', 'mb-3'],
             ['Table cells', '.5rem (sm too)'],
             ['Containers', '540 / 720 / 960 / 1140']
           ].each do |title, value| %>
          <div class="col">
            <div class="d-flex justify-content-between gap-3 py-2 border-bottom"><span><%= title %></span><code class="text-body-secondary"><%= value %></code></div>
          </div>
        <% end %>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- LAYOUT -->
  <section id="layout">
    <%== section_head.call('layout', 'Fixed dark header (2.8125rem) and a fixed sidebar (14.375rem, minified to 3.75rem). Below 768px the sidebar becomes a full-width offcanvas and header icons spread across a second row.') %>
    <div class="border rounded-3 overflow-hidden shadow">
      <div class="d-flex align-items-center px-3 text-white" style="height: 2.8125rem; font-size: 1.125rem; background: var(--gradient-header)">
        <img class="position-relative" style="max-height: 1.75rem; top: -0.25rem" src="/images/logos/white-on-transparent.png" alt="">
        <div class="ms-auto d-flex align-items-center">
          <span class="px-3"><i class="bi bi-search"></i></span>
          <span class="px-3 position-relative"><i class="bi bi-bell"></i><span class="position-absolute top-0 rounded-circle" style="right: .75rem; width: .5rem; height: .5rem; background: var(--gradient-active)"></span></span>
          <span class="px-3"><i class="bi bi-chat-left"></i></span>
          <span class="px-2"><span class="d-block rounded-circle" style="width: 1.75rem; height: 1.75rem; background: var(--bs-gray-600)"></span></span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="d-flex" style="min-height: 420px">
        <div class="d-none d-md-block flex-shrink-0 p-2" style="width: 14.375rem; background: var(--bs-gray-900)">
          <div class="d-flex align-items-center gap-2 py-2 px-3 text-white rounded" style="background: var(--gradient-active)"><i class="bi bi-house fs-4"></i><span>Home</span></div>
          <div class="d-flex align-items-center gap-2 py-2 px-3 text-white rounded"><i class="bi bi-newspaper fs-4" style="opacity: .35"></i><span>Dandelion Daily</span></div>
          <div class="d-flex align-items-center gap-2 py-2 px-3 text-white rounded bg-black"><i class="bi bi-calendar-event fs-4" style="opacity: .35"></i><span>Events</span><span class="ms-auto small opacity-50">hover</span></div>
          <div class="d-flex align-items-center gap-2 py-2 px-3 text-white rounded"><i class="bi bi-flag-fill fs-4" style="opacity: .35"></i><span class="flex-grow-1">Organisations</span><i class="bi bi-chevron-down small"></i></div>
          <div class="d-flex flex-column py-1 text-white" style="margin-left: 2.5625rem">
            <span class="py-1">Symbiota</span>
            <span class="py-1 opacity-50">All organisations</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="flex-grow-1 p-4 d-flex flex-column gap-3">
          <div class="spec">#content · padding 1.5625rem</div>
          <div class="row g-3 flex-grow-1">
            <% [['col-8', 'col-lg-8 · newsfeed'], ['col-4', 'col-lg-4 · sticky']].each do |col, label| %>
              <div class="<%= col %>">
                <div class="h-100 border rounded shadow-sm d-flex align-items-center justify-content-center text-center spec" style="background: repeating-linear-gradient(135deg, var(--color-canvas) 0 10px, #fff 10px 20px)"><%= label %></div>
              </div>
            <% end %>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- COMPONENTS -->
  <section id="components">
    <%== section_head.call('components') %>

    <div class="d-flex flex-column gap-3">
      <%== subhead.call('Buttons', 'Primary, secondary and danger are sheens over a transparent border: 135°, <code>--sheen-from</code> flat to halfway, then to <code>--sheen-to</code>. Fills (buttons, badges, progress bars, text-bg-primary and p.action) go from their 500 to the lighter 400, and on hover from the 600 to the 500; alerts, toasts and the AI well set their own pair. One rule draws every sheen. btn-warning is styled the same but not used yet; brand buttons like btn-signal stay flat.') %>
      <div class="border rounded p-4 d-flex flex-wrap gap-3 align-items-center">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="#components">Book tickets</a>
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="#components" style="--sheen-from: var(--theme-600); --sheen-to: var(--theme-500)">Hover</a>
        <a class="btn btn-outline-primary" href="#components">Outline primary</a>
        <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="#components">Secondary</a>
        <a class="btn btn-danger" href="#components">Delete</a>
        <a class="btn btn-signal" href="#components"><i class="bi bi-signal"></i> Signal</a>
      </div>
      <div class="d-flex flex-wrap gap-3 align-items-center px-4">
        <a class="btn btn-primary btn-sm" href="#components">btn-sm</a>
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="#components">btn</a>
        <a class="btn btn-primary btn-lg" href="#components">btn-lg</a>
      </div>
      <div class="spec">.btn · .875rem · padding .375rem .75rem · radius .25rem</div>
    </div>

    <div class="d-flex flex-column gap-3">
      <%== subhead.call('Badges', "Bootstrap's <code>.badge</code> with a <code>text-bg-*</code> colour, for counts, statuses, tags and amounts. Sized in em, so a badge scales with the text around it: small in a nav, bigger beside a heading. Pick the colour by what it means.") %>
      <div class="border rounded p-4 d-flex flex-column gap-3">
        <h4 class="m-0">Full moon gathering <span class="badge text-bg-yellow">Featured</span> <span class="badge text-bg-secondary">Locked</span></h4>
